============================== Reviewer Analysis ==============================
Root cause is mesh generation failure, and everything else is cascading from that.

- `log.blockMesh`: fatal error `Inconsistent number of faces between block pair 0 and 3` means your multi-block topology in `system/blockMeshDict` is not conformal at an interface (adjacent blocks have mismatched cell counts on the shared face).
- `log.topoSet`, `log.createPatch`, `log.pimpleFoam`: all fail with `Cannot find file "points" in directory "polyMesh"` because `blockMesh` never completed, so `constant/polyMesh/points` was never written.

How to fix (without changing required physics/BC/time settings)
- Keep domain and total resolution exactly as required (`0.20x0.20x0.01`, 2D, total `100x100x1`), but make block interfaces conformal.
- In your current 4-block layout, the shared face between block 0 and block 3 is along `y=0.01` from `x=0.00` to `0.09`; both touching blocks must have identical subdivisions along that shared edge. Right now they do not (block 0 has 45 cells in x; block 3 has 55 over a wider span), which causes the merge failure.
- Best robust approach: switch to a single hex block of `100 100 1` and create inlet using `topoSet + createPatch` (you already have these dictionaries). This preserves all user-required parameters and avoids block-interface mismatch entirely.
- If you keep multi-block mesh, enforce exact matching of cell counts on every shared face pair (same `Nx` and `Ny` on each interface, not just similar grading).

Additional consistency fixes needed after mesh succeeds
- Remove duplicate/incorrect field files under `system/` (`system/U`, `system/p`): OpenFOAM expects initial fields in `0/`. Having extra ones can confuse workflows.
- Make `0/U` and `0/p` patch names match the mesh boundary names exactly. Your mesh uses `base`, `sides`, `outlet`, `inlet`, `frontAndBack`, but `0/U` and `0/p` currently use `bottom` and `top`. Rename those entries to match the mesh patch names (e.g., `base` and `outlet`) while keeping the required BC types/values unchanged.
- Ensure your run script order is: `blockMesh` -> `topoSet` -> `createPatch -overwrite` -> `pimpleFoam` -> postProcess steps. Current logs indicate downstream tools run despite mesh failure; add stop-on-error behavior so pipeline halts immediately when `blockMesh` fails.

Expected outcome after correction
- `blockMesh` completes and writes `constant/polyMesh/points`.
- `topoSet/createPatch` can build inlet patch from the specified box.
- `pimpleFoam` starts normally with your required setup and post-processing can generate residuals/Courant/centerline outputs and PNG slices at requested times.
